Here are the sources to the "sdb" enhancements.  The files called "*.e" are
edit scripts for the files in question (*.c or *.h).  "bio.c" and "bio.h" are
what "old.c" and "old.h" were originally called; stick these versions in and
get rid of "old.c" and "old.h" - no guarantees, but they should make this
version of "sdb" work on a non-VM system.  Also, you can get rid of the file
"rdwr.c" in the original source, as it's just a copy of "fio.c".

	Guy Harris
